		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Where moringa comes from</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moringa grows in warm climates, where its small, tender leaves are harvested, gently dried and milled into a fine green powder.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The result is a vivid ingredient with a fresh, slightly grassy flavor that blends easily into everyday recipes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Simple ways to enjoy it</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whisk a spoonful into smoothies, stir it through yogurt or oat bowls, or fold it into pancake batter for a beautiful green color.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Keeping it fresh</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keep moringa sealed in its pouch or an airtight jar, away from heat and light, to protect its color and flavor.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
