	<item>
		<title><![CDATA[Storing your pantry powders]]></title>
		<link>/storing-your-pantry-powders/</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Cool, dry and dark</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Light, heat and moisture are the main enemies of plant powders. Keep them in airtight containers in a cool cupboard.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Always use a dry spoon to avoid clumping.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Stay organized</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Label your jars with the powder name and opening date, and keep your everyday favorites at the front of the shelf.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Simple tips for keeping your plant powders fresh, organized and ready for everyday use.]]></excerpt:encoded>
